Summary: Introduction to Kubernetes and OpenShift
Containers
•	A container is a packaged process that includes:
o	Application code
o	Runtime
o	Libraries
o	Dependencies
•	This allows the application to run consistently across different environments.
________________________________________
Containerization Benefits
Containerization helps solve common development problems such as:
•	Code portability – applications run the same way everywhere.
•	Consistency – development, testing, and production environments behave similarly.
•	Modularization – applications can be broken into smaller components (microservices).
•	Easier development and maintenance.
________________________________________
Challenges with Large Numbers of Containers
When many containers run together, it becomes difficult to manage:
•	Application availability
•	Networking between containers
•	Scaling applications
•	Container deployment and updates
To solve these problems, a container orchestration platform is required.
________________________________________
Kubernetes
•	Kubernetes is a container orchestration platform.
•	It helps manage containers at scale.
Key features include:
•	Automated deployment
•	Scaling applications
•	Load balancing
•	Self-healing containers
•	Networking between services
________________________________________
Pods
•	A Pod is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes.
•	A pod can contain:
o	One container
o	Or multiple tightly coupled containers
•	Containers inside a pod share:
o	Network
o	Storage
________________________________________
Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform (RHOCP)
•	OpenShift is an enterprise container platform built on top of Kubernetes.
•	It adds additional enterprise features such as:
o	Security enhancements
o	Developer tools
o	CI/CD integration
o	Monitoring and logging
o	Operator management
________________________________________
OpenShift Web Console
Most cluster tasks can be performed using the OpenShift Web Console, including:
•	Viewing logs
•	Monitoring metrics
•	Checking alerts
•	Accessing terminal sessions for nodes and pods
•	Managing applications and resources
The web console provides an easy graphical interface to manage the cluster.
________________________________________
✅ Key Idea:
•	Containers run applications
•	Kubernetes manages containers
•	OpenShift adds enterprise tools and a powerful web console on top of Kubernetes

